% .plan runs a query and writes its plan to standard output instead of its
% rows, even under -e, whose plans go to standard error; afterwards -e's
% explain callback is back in place, so the next query's plan goes to
% standard error again, followed by its rows.
edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- edge(X, Y), path(Y, Z).
